/T (A deque\(maxlen=7\) is useful for streaming readings: append each new value, maintain a running sum, and calculate an average once seven values are present. It uses O\(7\) = O\(1\) window space. A date-keyed dictionary offers average O\(1\) lookup by date, but chronological reports require sorting dates or maintaining a separate ordered sequence. A list stores n readings in O\(n\) space; a dictionary also uses O\(n\) space with higher per-entry overhead.)
/E (A deque\(maxlen=7\) is useful for streaming readings: append each new value, maintain a running sum, and calculate an average once seven values are present. It uses O\(7\) = O\(1\) window space. A date-keyed dictionary offers average O\(1\) lookup by date, but chronological reports require sorting dates or maintaining a separate ordered sequence. A list stores n readings in O\(n\) space; a dictionary also uses O\(n\) space with higher per-entry overhead.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
