/Title (A dictionary computes a hash for a key and uses it to locate a hash-table position. Collisions are resolved internally by Python. Lookup, insertion and update are O\(1\) average, so expected lookup time does not grow linearly with the number of keys; worst-case collision behaviour can be O\(n\).)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1484 0 R
/Next 1504 0 R
>>
endobj
1495 0 obj
<<
/Title (Python 3.7 and later guarantee dictionary insertion order. keys\(\) is a dynamic view of keys, values\(\) is a dynamic view of values, and items\(\) is a dynamic view of key-value pairs. Views reflect later dictionary changes.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1484 0 R
/Prev 1504 0 R
>>
endobj
