/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1501 0 R
/Next 1512 0 R
>>
endobj
1512 0 obj
<<
/Title (A list comprehension builds the complete list immediately and uses O\(n\) memory. A generator expression produces values lazily and usually uses O\(1\) auxiliary memory, excluding the input and any result being accumulated. Both require O\(n\) time to process n readings.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1501 0 R
/Prev 1511 0 R
>>
endobj
